<p>Narges Mohammadi, the imprisoned Iranian human rights activist and 2023 Nobel Peace Prize laureate, was transferred Friday from a prison in Zanjan, northwestern Iran, to a hospital after what her foundation called a “catastrophic deterioration” in her health, including two losses of consciousness and a severe cardiac crisis. The Narges Mohammadi Foundation said prison doctors determined her condition could not be managed inside the facility, while supporters said she remained in unstable condition and needed specialized treatment in Tehran. Her lawyers said they believed she suffered a heart attack in late March and that she appeared pale, underweight and unable to walk without a nurse when they visited her afterward. Mohammadi was arrested in Mashhad in December; her foundation dated the arrest to Dec. 12. She was later sentenced in February to more than seven years in prison.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/6TGkpOMioSIDNYCL_HAnz2B4jk0Tc8lKbtW6TQkuPK_EFAkHGTXPBPvJoWXNVOYjhqEPrH6v7GX8LR6yWnT-nJtXhHh9NwiLSTNEqJsqV9Uf3lR9jD-pRbq0J7oLLj6PC_C7ijj930gkWzrd7NOJSjqruStk2dxDUH846zqNjYUrl2pAz2Yx_yzbwhG9UCBjjiA' alt='Narges Mohammadi poses in an undated photo provided by her family. The Nobel laureate has suffered from heart ailments for years, according to her family.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Initial refusal: Lawyer Mostafa Nili said Mohammadi declined a hospital transfer after her first fainting spell, which he linked to a sudden drop in blood pressure, but she was moved after a second collapse and further deterioration.</li><li>Arrest allegations: Mohammadi’s family alleged she was struck in the head, neck and side during her December arrest; the cited report said Iranian authorities had not publicly responded to the allegation.</li><li>ICU status: Her husband said she was being treated in intensive care, while her brother Hamidreza Mohammadi told Radio Farda she was “on the brink of death”.</li></ul><blockquote>Her life is in Iran&#x27;s hands - Joergen Watne Frydnes</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Narges Mohammadi Foundation: The foundation said Mohammadi’s family saw the hospital transfer as a last-minute step that might prove too late and linked the crisis to 140 days of alleged systematic medical neglect. (<a href='https://www.brecorder.com/news/40419290/nobel-laureate-narges-mohammadi-hospitalised-in-iran-supporters'>Brecorder</a>)</li><li>Norwegian Nobel Committee: Committee chair Joergen Watne Frydnes urged Iranian authorities to release Mohammadi to her own medical team for urgent treatment. (<a href='https://www.livemint.com/news/world/her-life-is-in-irans-hands-nobel-committee-chief-says-as-jailed-activist-narges-mohammadi-is-hospitalised-11777742149114.html'>Livemint</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/video-nobel-laureate-mohammadi-in-iran-hospital-after-cardiac-crisis/'>Nobel laureate Mohammadi in Iran hospital after &#x27;cardiac crisis&#x27;</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/jailed-iranian-nobel-laureate-narges-mohammadi-hospitalised-at-very-high-risk-11441343#publisher=newsstand'>Jailed Iranian Nobel Laureate Narges Mohammadi Hospitalised, At &#x27;Very High Risk&#x27;</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/05/02/nx-s1-5808841/jailed-iranian-nobel-prize-winner-critical-condition'>Imprisoned Iranian Nobel Peace Prize winner in critical condition</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/iranian-nobel-peace-prize-laureate-narges-mohammadi-hospitalized-after-health-crisis-in-prison'>Iranian Nobel Peace Prize laureate Narges Mohammadi hospitalized after health crisis in prison</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c362pd8epw9o'>Concern for jailed Iranian Nobel laureate as family say health deteriorating</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='http://www.asiaone.com/asia/iranian-nobel-laureate-narges-mohammadi-hospitalised-after-health-crisis